RBF SURROGATE (EXPLORATORY, D4): churn, pca/12 qubits, 250/class, registered arm
==========================================================================
  For each quantum kernel: fit the closest RBF on training Gram matrices
  (no labels), run it through the same pipeline, compare out of sample.
  A difference near zero means the quantum kernel is functionally that RBF.

  setting      n  gamma (median)  in grid    d normAP                 95% CI          p
  angle-r1    20       2.818e-01 20/20         +0.0000     [-0.0057, +0.0057]     0.8983
  angle-r2    20       1.122e+00 20/20         -0.0162     [-0.0232, -0.0092]   1.05e-04
  iqp-r1      20       2.818e+00 20/20         +0.0852     [+0.0645, +0.1058]   1.91e-06
  iqp-r2      20       1.000e+01 20/20         -0.0493     [-0.0913, -0.0072]     0.0215

  By embedding family:
    angle  n=40  quantum minus surrogate: -0.0081 [-0.0131, -0.0030]   p 0.0037
           the quantum kernel is WORSE than its own closest RBF, so its structure is costing rather than earning.
    iqp    n=40  quantum minus surrogate: +0.0180 [-0.0132, +0.0492]   p 0.1701
           no detectable difference, but the interval is wide, so this is absence of evidence. More seeds, not a conclusion.

  Fitted gammas span 2.82e-01 to 1.00e+01; the registered classical RBF grid spans 1e-03 to 1e+02.
  80/80 surrogates use a gamma inside the range the classical arm already searched.

